From 5ee36bcaa95044db3761a47dc6c8acc668069fe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:13:31 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] AirPlayServer: don't open archives when clearing the photo
 asset cache

ClearPhotoAssetCache() lists special://temp/ only to delete the
airplayasset*.jpg/png files it finds there, but lists it with
DIR_FLAG_DEFAULTS. Without DIR_FLAG_NO_FILE_DIRS the listing runs
FilterFileDirectories(), which opens every archive in the directory to
decide whether to present it as a folder, reading each zip's full
central directory.

StartServer() calls StopServer(true), so this runs on every start and
stop of the AirPlay server, including at startup, and on the main
thread when the setting is toggled. With seven zip files of 65536 to
133000 entries each in special://temp/, every enable and disable froze
the GUI for about 4 seconds.

Pass DIR_FLAG_NO_FILE_DIRS, since only plain files are matched.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 xbmc/network/AirPlayServer.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/network/AirPlayServer.cpp b/xbmc/network/AirPlayServer.cpp
index 433a8c7c8d..326d02fefc 100644
--- a/xbmc/network/AirPlayServer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/network/AirPlayServer.cpp
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ void ClearPhotoAssetCache()
   CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "AIRPLAY: Cleaning up photoassetcache");
   // remove all cached photos
   CFileItemList items;
-  XFILE::CDirectory::GetDirectory("special://temp/", items, "", XFILE::DIR_FLAG_DEFAULTS);
+  XFILE::CDirectory::GetDirectory("special://temp/", items, "", XFILE::DIR_FLAG_NO_FILE_DIRS);
 
   for (int i = 0; i < items.Size(); ++i)
   {
